From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: allow 32 kHz playback

The SNES's DSP runs at 32 kHz (about 32040 on real consoles, which is
what Snes9x produces), and RetroArch upsampled it to 48000 because the
link could only carry 48000 and 44100. This adds 32000 the same way
1052 and 1053 added 44100:

- the longhand PRIMARY_MI2S_RX entry (the speakers) gains
  SNDRV_PCM_RATE_32000. The MI2S and CDC-DMA RX macros already list it,
  so the headphone port needs nothing;
- sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup() lets a frontend rate of exactly 32000
  through on PRIMARY_MI2S_RX and RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0, as it does 44100.
  Every other backend keeps the 48000 pin.

The bit clock needs no change: the DAI votes it from the stream at
hw_params (q6apm-lpass-dais MI2S clock control, with "bclk" on the
PRIMARY_MI2S_RX node), and 32000 x 2 x 16 = 1024000, which is
24.576 MHz / 24 and so in the same clock family as 48000. If q6prm
refuses it, the DAI logs "Unable to set rate".

The rest of the path already takes 32000: lpass-rx-macro (sr_val_tbl
{32000, 0x3}) for the headphones, and the aw88166 amps
(SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000_48000). The amps follow BCLK, as they do at 44100.
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-ports.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-ports.c
@@ -387,7 +387,8 @@
 		.playback = {
 			.stream_name = "Primary MI2S Playback",
 			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_48000 | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_44100 |
-				 SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000 | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_16000,
+				 SNDRV_PCM_RATE_32000 | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000 |
+				 SNDRV_PCM_RATE_16000,
 			.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE |
 				   SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE,
 			.channels_min = 1,
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -143,6 +143,13 @@
 		 */
 		if (fe_rate == 44100)
 			rate->min = rate->max = 44100;
+		/*
+		 * 32 kHz for the SNES, whose DSP runs at it. Both ports list
+		 * 32000, and the MI2S bit clock follows the stream, so this
+		 * is 1024000 - 24.576 MHz / 24, in the 48 kHz clock family.
+		 */
+		if (fe_rate == 32000)
+			rate->min = rate->max = 32000;
 		break;
 	default:
 		break;
